WHERE THE DISAGREEMENT STARTS AND STOPS (1400 B frames, 3 hops, 1/256):
  >= 5 Mbit/s (>=446 pps)   all three windows agree: present, 30/30.
  2 Mbit/s    (179 pps)     DISAGREEMENT STARTS. The 2 s edge count drops to 0.70 while the
                            3 s default and the 15 s table are still 1.00.
  1 Mbit/s    (89 pps)      the 2 s edge count is at 0.57 -- its own 50% point.
  250 kbit/s  (22 pps)      THE API DEFAULT crosses 50%: a flow sending continuously, delivered
                            with 0% loss, is absent from /ndt/get_detected_flow_data in half of
                            all one-second polls. The 15 s table still says 30/30.
  125 kbit/s  (11 pps)      default 0.40, edge 0.13, table still 1.00 -- the widest gap.
  60 kbit/s   (5 pps)       the 15 s table starts to fail too (0.93).
  <= 30 kbit/s (<=3 pps)    DISAGREEMENT STOPS by all three converging on "absent": edge 0.00,
                            default 0.10, table 0.43-0.67. Below this the twin simply does not
                            see the flow at all. (r30k/r15k are 3 and 1 pps; their table figures
                            differ in the wrong direction, which at ~0.02 samples/s is Poisson
                            noise on 30 polls, not a reversal -- do not read a trend into it.)

THE UNIT IS PACKETS, NOT BITS -- sweep B, same bandwidth, only the frame shrinking:
  1 Mbit/s @ 1400 B =    4465 pkts -> 1.07 samples/s -> 2 s edge 0.70, 3 s default 0.97
  1 Mbit/s @  600 B =   10417 pkts -> 2.21 samples/s -> 0.93, 1.00
  1 Mbit/s @  250 B =   25000 pkts -> 5.22 samples/s -> 0.97, 1.00
  1 Mbit/s @  100 B =   62499 pkts -> 12.4 samples/s -> 1.00, 1.00
  Same offered bandwidth in all four, 0% loss in all four. Visibility moved from 0.70 to 1.00
  on frame size alone. So every rate boundary above is a boundary in PACKETS PER SECOND
  (~22 pps for the API default's 50% point, ~89 pps for the edge count's) and moves by up to
  14x when a workload's frame size changes. Quoting the band in Mbit/s without the frame size
  is not transferable.
  p1400 also REPRODUCES sweep A's r1M cell 15 minutes later: edge 21/30 vs 17/30, default
  29/30 vs 26/30 -- same cell, N=2, consistent within Poisson noise.

CONTROLS: 12 quiet cells, one immediately before every load cell, same command, no traffic:
  0/8 on all three windows in 12 of 12. A decoy flow key (10.0.0.3 -> 10.0.0.4) that was never
  sent read absent in 100% of 456 polls while the real flow read present. Forced-green
  (20 Mbit/s) 30/30 on all three. The probe can say yes, can say no, and can tell two keys apart.
